### Roll Quality

**What this shows.** Every weapon with a copy left, one card per weapon: the weapon d2-perk-popularity scores the copy's version as (a family whose versions roll different trait pools is a card per pool, the pool in brackets), else its family. For each: its popularity on each side, the wishlists with rolls for it, then each copy, best PvE first, with its popularity scores, wishlist matches and perks.

**How it was derived.** Copies group by card; a family is the name without an Adept, Timelost or Harrowed suffix. A copy's popularity score on a side is the mean, over the perk columns d2-perk-popularity scores for its weapon, of its best perk's share of the column's votes against the column's most picked perk's (100% when it has the favourite in every column); its two trait columns count as one, scored by its best trait pair against the most picked pair, or each on its own when the weapon has no pair scores. Copies rank by that score, then wishlist matches, gear tier and age (lowest itemInstanceId). A copy's perks in a column are the ones it can switch to plus the one plugged. A copy completes a wishlist roll when it can equip every perk the roll names, trait perks in different trait sockets; a roll naming no perks fits every copy of its weapon, and a trash roll a copy fits marks it trash in that list instead. A weapon's ammo type is its definition's, its season comes from the release its definition's traits name, and its drop source is where its collection entry says it drops. RPM is a copy's rounds per minute (swords, fusion rifles and bows have none), and its kills are the count of the tracker plugged into its tracker socket, read as DIM reads it: PvE, PvP or Gambit.

**Reading it.** Nothing here is flagged: compare the copies and keep what you want; the first is the roll closest to what PvE players run. A perk's share is of its column's votes on that side, with its rank in the column (#1 the most picked; — for a perk players weren't seen with); when the copy lacks a column's favourite, it is named. A pair's share is of all the weapon's trait pairs. ★ marks a perk in a wishlist roll the copy completes, ☆ one a wishlist roll names that the copy doesn't complete. When a card's copies differ in element, rounds per minute, season or drop source, each copy names its own. "Trash in" names the lists that mark a copy's roll, or its whole weapon, as trash. "Missing wishlist entries" means no list has rolls for the weapon: judge it on popularity or light.gg (each card links its first copy's page). Low and very low confidence rest on a few copies: read those scores loosely.

