## Armor sets

**What this shows.** Each class's Legendary armor sets, with every Armor 3.0 piece by slot in score order, and which to purge; then the legacy pieces, from before Armor 3.0.

**How it was derived.** A piece's score is 3 × its set's first stat pick + 2 × the second + 1 × the third, on the best stats its own tuning socket (+5 to a stat it offers, -5 from another) and masterwork (+5 to each zero stat) can reach; a set without stat picks scores the stat total. Every gear tier competes on that score: a piece below Tier 5 has no tuning socket, so it scores on its own stats and masterwork. Each set keeps its grade's number of copies per slot ({% for g in grades %}{{ g.grade or g.label }} {{ g.slot_cap }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}), best score first, ties to the older copy; the rest are purged unless a three-stat build needs them (see Builds). A piece with the same stats and tuning stats as an older copy of its set is an exact copy and is purged. Legacy pieces, from before Armor 3.0 (no gear tier, set bonus or tuning socket), are always purged. Grades, ranks and stat picks come from your armor preferences. Each set's bonuses are Bungie's, with their grade, rank and note on The Aegis's sheet where it has them.

**Reading it.** Purge the pieces marked so; "Kept for" names the builds a piece past its cap stays for. Stats are base stats; "tunes" names the stats a piece's tuning socket can raise, and "adds" what the swap the score uses adds to it.

