## Builds

**What this shows.** For each class, the three-stat builds the kept armor leaves short of 100, and the pieces kept past their set's cap so that a build reaches 100.

**How it was derived.** For each of the 20 combinations of three of the six stats, the best kept Legendary piece in each slot, of any gear tier (the highest lowest-of-the-three, then the highest total, then the lowest itemInstanceId), adding up raw stats with no tuning or masterwork. Exotics are left out. A build is covered when each of its three stats totals at least 100. When the kept pieces leave a build short, a piece past its set's cap that takes it to 100 is kept: one piece when one is enough, else two from different slots; the better set wins first (grade, then rank), then the higher new lowest stat, then the score, then the lower itemInstanceId.

**Reading it.** A short build lacks pieces strong in its stats: keep or farm pieces that are.

