## Preferences

**What this shows.** Everything the app stores from you: your armor preferences (each armor set's preferred stats and grade, in rank order within the grade, then each exotic's preferred stats) and the wishlists weapon rolls are scored against.

**How it was derived.** Read as stored in the armor_preference table. You set them in the preference editor (`d2-report --edit-armor-prefs`) or when a run asks about a new set or exotic; a set or exotic without an entry of yours gets the app's shipped default, added when the database opens. An exotic's class comes from the manifest. The wishlists are the app's defaults plus any you added with `d2-report --add-wishlist`, read from the wishlist_preference table.

**Reading it.** These drive the armor pruning: a set's grade sets how many copies it keeps per slot ({% for g in grades %}{{ g.grade or g.label }} {{ g.slot_cap }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}), its rank orders it within the grade (the order the sets are listed in; a build's rescue prefers the better set), and a piece scores 3 × its first preferred stat + 2 × the second + 1 × the third.

